--

COPY public."ChadhavaListing" (id, title, description, location, image, price, "offerPrice", "gstPercentage", "gstInclusive", "createdAt", significance, benefits, "secondaryTabLabel", media) FROM stdin;
cms73kj4y0007tm0163hd1dl5	Mor Pankh Chadhava at Khatu Shaym Ji	Mor Pankh (Peacock Feather) is a sacred and auspicious offering to Khatu Shyam Ji, symbolizing devotion, purity, and divine grace.\n\nIt is believed that offering Mor Pankh pleases Shyam Baba and invites His blessings of peace, prosperity, and protection. The peacock feather represents beauty, wisdom, and victory over negativity, encouraging devotees to surrender their worries at the Lord's feet.\n\nDevotees offer Mor Pankh with faith to seek success, happiness, and the fulfillment of heartfelt wishes. This sacred chadhava is especially cherished in the worship of Khatu Shyam Ji, bringing spiritual upliftment, positive energy, and the blessings of Shyam Baba into one's life.	Sikar, Rajasthan	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1uAV57qteFe80jyupi-8HOiybPmW-N_-J&sz=w1000	101	51	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.523	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj540008tm01niic203u	Ittar Chadhava at Khatu Shaym Ji	Ittar (Sacred Fragrance) is a divine and auspicious offering to Khatu Shyam Ji, symbolizing purity, devotion, and heartfelt reverence.\n\nThe soothing fragrance of Ittar is offered as a mark of love and respect to Shyam Baba, creating a spiritually uplifting atmosphere during worship. It represents the devotee's sincere prayers, pure intentions, and the desire to remain connected with the Lord's divine presence.\n\nDevotees offer Ittar to seek peace, prosperity, and the fulfillment of their wishes. This sacred chadhava is believed to attract Khatu Shyam Ji's blessings, bringing positivity, happiness, and spiritual harmony into one's life.	Sikar, Rajasthan	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1ioomt1c9njS_FPOSBmltd0gYQob_rLvV&sz=w1000	101	51	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.529	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj570009tm01bcg8uewc	Gulab Chadhava at Khatu Shaym Ji	Gulab (Rose) is a sacred and beautiful offering to Khatu Shyam Ji, symbolizing pure devotion, love, and unwavering faith.\n\nThe fragrance and beauty of fresh roses express a devotee's heartfelt prayers and deep reverence for Shyam Baba. Offering Gulab signifies surrendering one's ego and seeking divine grace with a pure and loving heart.\n\nDevotees offer Gulab Chadhava to pray for happiness, peace, prosperity, and the fulfillment of their sincere wishes. This auspicious offering is believed to attract Khatu Shyam Ji's blessings, filling life with positivity, spiritual joy, and divine protection.	Sikar, Rajasthan	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1FKA0hWlrU5O1_dY_u79dMAizrUG76N6g&sz=w1000	101	51	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.531	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj59000atm01a6hyl1hg	Combo Chadhava at Khatu Shaym Ji	The Mor Pankh, Ittar, and Gulab Chadhava Combo is a sacred and auspicious offering to Khatu Shyam Ji, symbolizing devotion, purity, love, and divine grace.\n\nThis special combination brings together the spiritual significance of the peacock feather, the soothing fragrance of Ittar, and the beauty of fresh roses, expressing complete surrender and heartfelt devotion to Shyam Baba. Each offering represents faith, respect, and the desire to receive the Lord's blessings with a pure heart.\n\nDevotees offer this sacred combo to seek peace, prosperity, success, protection, and the fulfillment of their heartfelt wishes. It is believed that this divine chadhava pleases Khatu Shyam Ji and invites His blessings of happiness, positivity, spiritual growth, and everlasting grace into one's life.	Sikar, Rajasthan	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1ayzaj7b6IdNmq5Hk5K0VPqj9EGjh5uUE&sz=w1000	301	151	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.533	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5b000btm01uex84vkx	Dhatura Chadhava at Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga	Dhatura (Thorn Apple) is a sacred and powerful offering to Lord Shiva, believed to be very dear to Him.Dhatura (Thorn Apple) is a sacred and powerful offering to Lord Shiva, believed to be very dear to Him.\nIt symbolizes the removal of negativity, poison, and harmful energies from life. Offering Dhatura represents surrendering ego, anger, and inner impurities at Shivji’s feet.\nDevotees offer it to seek protection, strength, and courage during difficult times. This chadhava is especially auspicious in Shiv puja, bringing divine blessings and spiritual growth.	Mandhata, Madhya Pradesh	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=10u10vKZTvT7j3Mz8CP3fNjQN0LUpJg77&sz=w1000	201	151	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.535	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5d000ctm01sn4tvnw4	Bel Patra Aur Jal Chadhava at Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga	On Mondays, offering Bel Patra and Jal to Lord Shiva is considered highly auspicious and spiritually powerful.\n\nBel Patra symbolizes pure devotion and surrender, while Jal (holy water) represents calmness, purity, and the soothing of life’s struggles.\n\nTogether, they express faith, gratitude, and deep reverence toward Shivji.\n\nThis sacred Monday offering is believed to remove negativity, fulfill heartfelt wishes, and bring peace, positivity, and inner balance into one’s life.	Mandhata, Madhya Pradesh	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1TLpzBEqqOubSKGMQqzmfBay_U7LaSXsD&sz=w1000	201	151	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.537	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5f000dtm01ng8qjrlj	Combo Chadhava at Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga	This Chadhava Basket includes Dhatura, fresh flowers, fruits, sweets, and Chandan, carefully selected for Shiv puja.\n\nEach item carries deep spiritual significance and is considered dear to Lord Shiva. Dhatura represents protection and removal of negativity, while Chandan symbolizes peace and purity. Fruits and sweets express gratitude and devotion offered with a pure heart.\n\nThis complete basket is ideal for temple visits, special pujas, and sacred rituals, helping seek divine blessings, strength, prosperity, and inner peace.	Mandhata, Madhya Pradesh	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1qremlQU0KqwLnTeGC9I-wVxwKr4g4AMZ&sz=w1000	401	251	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.539	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5h000etm0175hgf0ky	Dhatura Chadhava at Trimbakeshwar Jyotirlinga	Dhatura (Thorn Apple) is a sacred and powerful offering to Lord Shiva, believed to be very dear to Him.Dhatura (Thorn Apple) is a sacred and powerful offering to Lord Shiva, believed to be very dear to Him.\nIt symbolizes the removal of negativity, poison, and harmful energies from life. Offering Dhatura represents surrendering ego, anger, and inner impurities at Shivji’s feet.\nDevotees offer it to seek protection, strength, and courage during difficult times. This chadhava is especially auspicious in Shiv puja, bringing divine blessings and spiritual growth.	Nashik, Maharashtra	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1HRs7dvjxyjz2VDRBoo9R4rEviY01qqjO&sz=w1000	201	151	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.541	\N	\N	\N	\N
