cms73kj5v000ktm017ih661p5	Kumkum Chadhava at Shree Ambabai Temple	Kumkum Chadhava is a sacred and auspicious offering in Hindu worship.\n\nKumkum symbolizes shakti (divine energy), prosperity, and marital bliss. Offering it expresses devotion, respect, and gratitude toward the deity.\n\nThis chadhava is believed to attract positivity, protection, success, and divine blessings, especially in Devi and Ganpati puja.	Kolhapur, Maharashtra	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1vbu7Azu0B9SmgoIBCCLlnyn-Fm_p8USk&sz=w1000	351	251	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.555	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5x000ltm01taowopm5	Chunni Chadhava at Shree Ambabai Temple	Offering a Chunni in puja is a sacred gesture of devotion, especially to the Divine Mother.\n\nIt symbolizes respect, honor, and surrender at the feet of the Goddess. Draping a Chunni represents offering sacred vastra and seeking protection and blessings.\n\nThis auspicious chadhava is believed to attract prosperity, positivity, and the grace of the Divine Feminine into life.	Kolhapur, Maharashtra	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1BrCdlssQnaw-lZ4E6Oivts5S6_AjOQ9g&sz=w1000	351	251	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.557	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj5z000mtm01mavr5bur	Saree & Blouse Piece Chadhava at Shree Ambabai Temple	Offering a Blouse Piece on Friday is considered highly auspicious, especially in Devi puja.\n\nIt symbolizes respect, gratitude, and devotion toward the Divine Mother. Presenting a blouse piece reflects the tradition of offering sacred vastra (clothing) as a mark of honor and surrender.\n\nOn Friday, this offering is believed to attract blessings of prosperity, harmony, protection, and divine feminine grace into one’s life.	Kolhapur, Maharashtra	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1LevpwI8Eeys2Q9i644_nImmQpsqTP4Xu&sz=w1000	501	351	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.56	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj64000otm019487z295	Kala Til Chadhava at Shani Dev Temple	Black Sesame Seeds (Kale Til) are considered a powerful and sacred offering in Hindu rituals.\n\nThey symbolize protection, purification, and the removal of negative energies and karmic obstacles. Kale Til are often offered in prayers for peace, ancestral blessings, and spiritual balance.\n\nThis chadhava is believed to bring stability, strength, positivity, and divine protection into life.	Hathla, Gujarat	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1XEIUBTewpQF5kQto1Z-N5vu6P6F8x54Q&sz=w1000	151	101	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.564	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj61000ntm01hhl99uku	Oil Chadhava at Shani Dev Temple	Til ka Tel (Sesame Oil) is a sacred and powerful element used in Hindu puja rituals.\n\nIt symbolizes purification, protection, and the removal of negative energies. Lighting a diya with Til ka Tel is believed to reduce obstacles and bring spiritual strength.\n\nThis auspicious offering invites peace, stability, positivity, and divine blessings into life.	Hathla, Gujarat	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1aeUfURLrlckDj9BdFb5LfybcRySasxoW&sz=w1000	151	101	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.562	\N	\N	\N	\N
cms73kj69000qtm01v7ijgmtm	Oil & Kala Til Combo Chadhava at Shani Dev Temple	Oil & Sesame Seed (Til) is a sacred and powerful offering in Hindu rituals.\n\nTil symbolizes purification and protection, while oil represents the removal of negativity and obstacles. Together, they are often used for diya lighting and special prayers for peace and stability.\n\nThis chadhava is believed to attract strength, protection, positivity, and divine blessings into life.	Hathla, Gujarat	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1PL9hiY9M2tNNRvqWm_yujs56qDixv0Yp&sz=w1000	351	251	0	t	2026-07-30 05:52:55.57	\N	\N	\N	\N
