COPY public."PujaListing" (id, title, description, image, price, category, "createdAt", "templeName", "templeLocation", significance, benefits, "secondaryTabLabel", media) FROM stdin;
cms7542y00003mr01pv73y2n1	Ashwini Nakshatra Shanti puja	Ashvini Nakshatra Puja is an elaborate Vedic ritual performed to harmonize the energies of Ashvini Nakshatra and neutralize its malefic effects, especially those stemming from its association with the planet Ketu. This puja is essential for individuals born under Ashvini Nakshatra or those experiencing challenges attributed to it, such as health issues, anxiety, loneliness, delays in accomplishments, and emotional instability.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1mwmK8kAt608yZzKAjlHiCB1kjXu_gJD-&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.272	\N	\N	Performed for those born under Ashwini Nakshatra to harmonize its energies and pacify the malefic influence of Ketu.	Relieves anxiety and emotional instability\nReduces health-related struggles\nRemoves delays in accomplishments\nEases feelings of loneliness\nRestores emotional balance and confidence	\N	\N
cms75430r0023mr01zxbpnxhf	Baglamukhi Anushthan	Baglamukhi Anushthan is a powerful ritual honoring Goddess Baglamukhi, the eighth Mahavidya, known for granting victory, protection, and empowerment. It includes Ganesh Puja, Navgraha Puja, chanting 125,000 mantras, offerings, and homam. Devotees perform it to overcome enemies, remove malefic influences, achieve success, and gain strength against life’s challenges.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1hr-xDzN1lgFiT_a5KETB6jJHlLlu_bv4&sz=w1000	8500	Vedic Anushthan	2026-07-30 06:36:07.372	\N	\N	Honors Goddess Baglamukhi, the eighth Mahavidya, through an elaborate ritual of extensive mantra chanting and homam.	Grants protection from enemies\nRemoves malefic influences\nBuilds strength against challenges\nSupports victory and success\nEmpowers confidence	\N	\N
cms75430u0026mr01un0kiucc	Mahamrityunjaya Anushthan	Mahamritunjya Anushthan is a sacred Hindu ritual dedicated to Lord Shiva, especially involving the chanting and worship of the Mahamrityunjaya Mantra, known as the great victory over death. This puja is performed to relieve pain and suffering caused by serious illnesses, to prevent premature death, and to overcome fears related to mortality. The mantra and the associated rituals are believed to provide protection from negative planetary influences, evil spirits, and disasters, while promoting longevity, health, happiness, and prosperity.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1W6f7fCqWDHrLeFS8Pv94ynib9pmCJeGn&sz=w1000	8500	Vedic Anushthan	2026-07-30 06:36:07.375	\N	\N	Dedicated to Lord Shiva through chanting of the Mahamrityunjaya Mantra to overcome fear of mortality and illness.	Relieves pain from serious illness\nHelps prevent premature death\nProtects from negative planetary influences\nPromotes longevity and health\nBrings happiness and prosperity	\N	\N
cms75430y0029mr012567bbya	Nav Chandi Path	Nav Chandi Path, also known as Navchandi Puja or Yagna, is a sacred Hindu ritual dedicated to Goddess Chandi, the fierce form of Maa Durga, and is primarily performed during Navratri. The term "Nav Chandi" signifies the nine-fold recitation of the Durga Saptashati or Devi Mahatmyam, a scripture from the Markandeya Purana that recounts the victory of the Goddess over demonic forces and celebrates the triumph of divine energy over evil.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1HHnEU07nEKaymkQ71_RuTE5sgrQMOKwB&sz=w1000	8500	Vedic Anushthan	2026-07-30 06:36:07.378	\N	\N	A nine-fold recitation of the Durga Saptashati honoring Goddess Chandi, primarily performed during Navratri.	Invokes divine protection from negative forces\nCelebrates the triumph of good over evil\nStrengthens spiritual energy\nSupports overall well-being\nBrings positivity into life	\N	\N
cms754311002cmr010zm46wwd	Navgrah Shanti Anushthan	Navgrah Shanti Anushthan is a comprehensive Vedic ritual performed to seek the blessings of all nine planetary deities, known as Navagrahas, in order to neutralize malefic planetary influences and promote overall prosperity, harmony, and peace in one's life. This Anushthan is especially recommended when multiple planetary doshas or afflictions are present in one's horoscope, affecting health, relationships, finances, or career.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1iTzSM_1kOdWHvt6UjqhwXSFICJJ8ho48&sz=w1000	8500	Vedic Anushthan	2026-07-30 06:36:07.381	\N	\N	Seeks the blessings of all nine Navagrahas to neutralize multiple planetary doshas at once.	Reduces combined planetary afflictions\nImproves health, career, and relationships\nRestores overall harmony\nPromotes prosperity\nBrings peace of mind	\N	\N
cms754315002fmr017hlk9bqz	Shat Chandi Path	Shat Chandi Path is an intense and ancient Vedic ritual centered on the complete recitation of the 700 verses of the Durga Saptashati (Devi Mahatmyam) from the Markandeya Purana, divided into thirteen chapters. This anushthan is performed to invoke Goddess Durga in her most fierce and protective forms, aiming to eliminate obstacles, defeat negative energies, remove planetary doshas (such as Rahu-Ketu or Shani Dosh), and fulfill desires related to health, prosperity, courage, and harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1INfrR0XX0JMnru42SnbmaXn0Z28_WweH&sz=w1000	8500	Vedic Anushthan	2026-07-30 06:36:07.385	\N	\N	Complete recitation of the 700-verse Durga Saptashati to invoke Goddess Durga's fiercest, most protective forms.	Eliminates obstacles and negative energies\nRemoves planetary doshas like Rahu-Ketu or Shani Dosh\nFulfills wishes for health and prosperity\nBuilds courage\nRestores harmony	\N	\N
cms754318002imr01ceh1hmu0	Brihaspati puja	Brihaspati Puja is a Hindu worship ritual held mainly on Thursdays (Brihaspativar, also called Guruvar) to honor Brihaspati, the divine teacher or ‘Guru’ of the gods, who corresponds to the planet Jupiter in Vedic astrology. Devotees dedicate the day to Lord Vishnu and Brihaspati, wear yellow clothes, offer yellow flowers, fruits, and recite special prayers and mantras seeking wisdom, academic growth, spiritual knowledge, good health, and prosperity.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1AFC4PctHGxDI_tBhyAeKlc3yCihQH45Z&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Shanti Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.388	\N	\N	Honors Brihaspati (Jupiter), the divine Guru of the gods, typically performed on Thursdays.	Enhances wisdom and academic growth\nBoosts spiritual knowledge\nImproves health\nAttracts prosperity\nStrengthens guidance and clarity	\N	\N
cms75431c002lmr018yllmdbe	Chandra Puja	Chandra Puja is a significant Hindu ritual devoted to Lord Chandra, the Moon God, who is one of the Navagrahas (nine planets) in Vedic tradition. Revered for governing the mind, emotions, and intuition, Chandra is worshipped to bring peace, emotional stability, and spiritual renewal to devotees. The ceremony typically takes place during Chandra Darshan, the sighting of the new moon, when prayers and offerings are made to seek his blessings for prosperity, mental strength, and harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1Gk1meCWPI_Fx1bmDP_qae1ch7honYUuC&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Shanti Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.392	\N	\N	Dedicated to Chandra (Moon), governing mind, emotions, and intuition, often performed during Chandra Darshan.	Brings emotional stability\nPromotes inner peace\nSupports spiritual renewal\nStrengthens mental resilience\nAttracts prosperity and harmony	\N	\N
cms7542y70006mr01y9fnhckx	Ashlesha Nakshatra Shanti Puja	Ashlesha Nakshatra Shanti Puja is a traditional Vedic ritual aimed at pacifying the malefic effects associated with Ashlesha Nakshatra, which is ruled by the serpent deity and governed by planet Mercury (Budh). This Nakshatra is known for its complex and mysterious energies, often causing mental restlessness, indecision, emotional instability, and various kinds of doshas if afflicted in one’s horoscope.​	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1Z8bEpkNryI2l72P-EINy6h7IsiT7Ojt5&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.279	\N	\N	Pacifies the complex, Mercury-ruled energies of Ashlesha Nakshatra, associated with the serpent deity.	Calms mental restlessness and indecision\nImproves clarity in decision-making\nReduces nakshatra-related doshas\nRestores emotional stability\nSupports overall well-being	\N	\N
cms7542yc0009mr0115w33omh	Magha Nakshatra Shanti Puja	Magha Nakshatra Puja is a Vedic ritual honoring ancestors and reducing negative influences linked to Magha Nakshatra, ruled by Ketu. It seeks blessings, protection, and guidance from forefathers, fostering spiritual growth and removing ancestral obstacles. The puja supports leadership, career progress, and financial prosperity, while enhancing confidence, mental clarity, and emotional balance. It is especially beneficial for those born under Magha Nakshatra or facing challenges in career, social standing, or family harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=107XQ9xL7RsuwzkB2NzpdXbhzRo5oDLYz&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.285	\N	\N	Honors ancestors and reduces the Ketu-linked negative influences tied to Magha Nakshatra.	Invokes ancestral blessings and protection\nSupports leadership and career growth\nStrengthens financial prosperity\nEnhances confidence and mental clarity\nRestores emotional balance	\N	\N
cms7542yh000cmr01y7fl7d4b	Jyestha Nakshatra Shanti Puja	Jyeshta Nakshatra Puja is a sacred Vedic ritual performed to pacify the challenging and intense energies of Jyeshta Nakshatra, ruled by planet Mercury (Budh). This nakshatra is linked to emotional depth, ego, and karmic challenges that can cause hurdles in career, family relationships, mental peace, and decision-making. The puja aims to balance these energies, removing obstacles related to health, profession, and emotional instability, while promoting mental clarity, confidence, and harmony in life.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1fMX_2nC9eFl32cszE6VgyQwwb-ZHk8Kl&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.289	\N	\N	Balances the intense, Mercury-ruled energies of Jyestha Nakshatra tied to ego and karmic challenges.	Removes obstacles in career and profession\nEases family relationship tensions\nRestores mental peace\nImproves decision-making\nBuilds confidence and harmony	\N	\N
cms7542yk000fmr013plrkbzv	Moola Nakshatra Shanti Puja	Moola Nakshatra Shanti Puja is a sacred Vedic ritual performed to mitigate the challenges and malefic effects associated with Moola Nakshatra, ruled by the goddess Nirriti and governed by the planet Ketu. This nakshatra is known for its transformative energy, which can sometimes lead to difficulties such as obstacles in health, prosperity, and emotional stability if afflicted in a person's horoscope.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1s-b8d4F6BxU4jfmkdY3BBHmFAsZYRfkO&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.293	\N	\N	Mitigates the transformative, Ketu-ruled energies of Moola Nakshatra, governed by the goddess Nirriti.	Reduces health-related obstacles\nSupports financial prosperity\nRestores emotional stability\nRemoves nakshatra-linked doshas\nEncourages overall well-being	\N	\N
cms7542yo000imr015vk35e2r	Revati Nakshatra Shanti Puja	Revati Nakshatra Puja is a sacred Vedic ritual performed to alleviate doshas and negative effects of Revati Nakshatra, ruled by Mercury and associated with deity Pushan. It promotes inner peace, mental clarity, emotional stability, and overall well-being, especially for those born under Revati or affected by related planetary afflictions. The puja includes Ganesh Pujan, Matra Pujan, Punyavachan, Kalash Sthapana, Raksha Vidhan, Navagraha Puja, and chanting of stotras and ashtottara namavali, culminating in a homa (fire ritual) that dispels negativity and invokes divine blessings for prosperity and spiritual growth.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1LVpw3sVRK6g7_QXiENLQL2TP8ryIo3tr&sz=w1000	8500	Nakshatra Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.296	\N	\N	Alleviates doshas linked to Revati Nakshatra through an elaborate multi-stage Vedic ceremony culminating in a homa.	Promotes inner peace and mental clarity\nRestores emotional stability\nDispels negative planetary influences\nInvokes blessings for prosperity\nSupports spiritual growth	\N	\N
cms7542ys000lmr01nu8hxxgw	Chandra Ketu Dosh Puja	Chandra Ketu Dosh Puja is a ritual performed to reduce the malefic effects of the conjunction of Moon (Chandra) and Ketu in one's horoscope. This puja includes chanting bija mantras of Chandra (11,000 times) and Ketu (17,000 times), Vedic rituals like Homa (Havan) using sacred offerings, and worship of associated deities. It aims to pacify dosha energies, remove planetary imbalances, and restore emotional balance and spiritual harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1nCJDPbAuh2it2Wj49PGzDyf6P-RTCTKQ&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.301	\N	\N	Reduces the malefic effects of a Moon-Ketu conjunction in the horoscope through mantra chanting and homa.	Pacifies dosha energies from the Chandra-Ketu conjunction\nRestores emotional balance\nRemoves planetary imbalances\nEncourages spiritual harmony\nReduces related anxiety and mental unrest	\N	\N
cms7542yw000omr014tm9jjoo	Chandra Rahu Dosh Puja	Chandra Rahu Dosh Puja is performed to neutralize the negative effects caused by the conjunction of Moon (Chandra) and Rahu in a horoscope, which can lead to emotional instability, mental stress, and confusion. This puja involves rituals such as Ganesh Puja, Navagraha Puja, chanting of bija mantras for Chandra and Rahu, and Homa. It helps relieve anxiety, enhances mental clarity, and promotes inner peace by balancing the energies of the Moon and Rahu.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=14p-mV8RjuEZoXLy5NvD1cuP7oQyNKf2H&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.305	\N	\N	Neutralizes the negative effects of a Moon-Rahu conjunction that can cause emotional instability and confusion.	Relieves anxiety and mental stress\nEnhances mental clarity\nPromotes inner peace\nBalances Moon and Rahu energies\nReduces confusion and emotional turbulence	\N	\N
cms7542z1000rmr017nhd72sw	Gandmool Nakshatra Dosh Puja	Gandmool Nakshatra Dosh Puja is a sacred ritual performed to nullify the negative effects of Gandmool dosh arising from birth under specific nakshatras such as Ashwini, Ashlesha, Magha, Revati, Jyestha, and Moola. This dosh often causes difficulties in health, family relationships, financial stability, and overall well-being. The puja involves mantras chanting, offering prayers to planetary and nakshatra deities, using 27 types of leaves and water from 27 places in a detailed homa ceremony. It seeks divine blessings to remove obstacles, protect ancestors' blessings, and usher in prosperity and harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1xMFkcwADjTSMfVyZJtGl9f95f1ZB2d0l&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.309	\N	\N	Nullifies Gandmool dosh arising from birth under specific nakshatras, using an elaborate 27-leaf, 27-water-source homa.	Removes obstacles in health and family relationships\nStrengthens financial stability\nProtects ancestral blessings\nUshers in prosperity and harmony\nReduces nakshatra-linked hardships	\N	\N
cms7542z6000umr017v5gun62	Guru Ketu Dosh Puja	Guru Ketu Dosh Puja is a Vedic ritual performed to neutralize the adverse effects caused by the conjunction of Jupiter (Guru) and Ketu in a birth chart, often known as Chandal Dosh. This dosh can create confusion, poor judgment, career obstacles, and spiritual disconnect. The puja includes traditional rituals, chanting of mantras, homam, and worship to harmonize the energies of Guru and Ketu. It fosters mental clarity, strengthens decision-making, and restores inner peace and spiritual growth.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1pFkfUa5y7CNzWfXrzDOnBPK9rmGUWH8_&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.314	\N	\N	Neutralizes the adverse effects of a Jupiter-Ketu conjunction, known as Chandal Dosh, through traditional rituals and homam.	Improves clarity in judgment\nReduces career obstacles\nStrengthens decision-making\nRestores inner peace\nSupports spiritual growth	\N	\N
cms7542za000xmr010sdt560k	Guru Rahu Dosh Puja	Guru Rahu Dosh Puja is performed to neutralize the negative effects caused by the conjunction of Jupiter (Guru) and Rahu in the horoscope. This dosh can cause mental confusion, poor decision-making, career and relationship issues, and instability. The puja involves mantra chanting, homa, and rituals to strengthen Jupiter’s positive influence and reduce Rahu's malefic impact. It helps bring clarity in judgment, emotional stability, and overall harmony.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=18PvD4a7zNs1D6jtuvvvhGJIRU1PiZaCv&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.319	\N	\N	Neutralizes the negative effects of a Jupiter-Rahu conjunction in the horoscope through mantra chanting and homa.	Improves clarity in judgment\nReduces career and relationship issues\nStabilizes emotions\nStrengthens Jupiter's positive influence\nRestores overall harmony	\N	\N
cms7542ze0010mr01lu4cxa6e	Kalsarp Dosh Nivaran Puja	Kalsarp Dosh Nivaran Puja is a sacred Vedic ritual performed to nullify the adverse effects of Kalsarp Dosh, which occurs when all seven planets are hemmed between Rahu and Ketu in the horoscope. This dosh can cause obstacles in career, health, marriage, finances, and overall life progress. The puja includes chanting powerful mantras, performing fire rituals, and worshipping Lord Shiva and other deities to pacify the dosh. It clears negative energies, removes hurdles, improves mental peace, enhances career growth, stabilizes health, and brings harmony in relationships.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1rvBGVKwuZPHzxhqhH6iYDcSNFp1Yp7ud&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.323	\N	\N	Nullifies Kalsarp Dosh, formed when all planets are hemmed between Rahu and Ketu, through mantra chanting and fire rituals honoring Lord Shiva.	Clears obstacles in career and finances\nImproves marital harmony\nRemoves negative energies\nEnhances mental peace\nStabilizes health	\N	\N
cms7542zi0013mr01ixxqelor	Mangal Ketu Dosh Puja	Mangal Ketu Dosh Puja is a Vedic ritual aimed at reducing the harmful effects of the conjunction of Mars (Mangal) and Ketu in a person's horoscope. This dosh can lead to aggression, emotional instability, confusion, and unexpected obstacles in life. The puja includes chanting mantras, performing homa, and other sacred rituals to calm the intense energies of Mars and Ketu. It helps bring mental clarity, emotional balance, harmony in relationships, and protection from sudden mishaps.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1USVpa17AooHg1E_Drs-IGZjRV0PNMoiK&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.326	\N	\N	Reduces the harmful effects of a Mars-Ketu conjunction in the horoscope through mantra chanting and homa.	Calms aggression and emotional instability\nReduces sudden obstacles\nRestores mental clarity\nImproves relationship harmony\nProvides protection from mishaps	\N	\N
cms7542zm0016mr01wikddq8o	Kemdrum Yog Dosh	Kemdrum Yog Dosh arises when the Moon is isolated in the 2nd and 12th houses, without neighboring planets to support it. This inauspicious dosh can cause mental stress, emotional turbulence, loneliness, financial difficulties, and obstacles in life. Since the Moon governs emotions, its weakness affects peace of mind and stability. Performing Kemdrum Yog Dosh Puja with rituals and mantra chanting strengthens the Moon’s positive influence, promoting emotional balance, clarity, and prosperity.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=16kQBUPSSfhrhpsXp2x7S-QTlAo0VMkaf&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.33	\N	\N	Strengthens a weak, isolated Moon responsible for Kemdrum Yog Dosh through rituals and mantra chanting.	Reduces mental stress and loneliness\nEases financial difficulties\nRestores emotional balance\nImproves clarity of mind\nEncourages prosperity	\N	\N
cms7542zq0019mr01v9pzy0jt	Mangal Rahu Dosh Puja	Mangal Rahu Dosh Puja is a Vedic ritual to mitigate the negative effects caused by the conjunction of Mars (Mangal) and Rahu in the horoscope, known as Angarak Dosh. This dosh often results in aggression, impulsiveness, accidents, disputes, and mental unrest. The puja includes chanting mantras, homa rituals, and worship to pacify these planets, calm the mind, and restore balance. It helps in improving mental focus, emotional control, relationships, and overall success in life.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1PbGni7pDdjcX04PkqnhWK2Xc_sfkt8f0&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.335	\N	\N	Mitigates the effects of a Mars-Rahu conjunction, known as Angarak Dosh, through mantra chanting and homa.	Reduces aggression and impulsiveness\nLowers risk of disputes and accidents\nImproves mental focus\nRestores emotional control\nEnhances relationship harmony	\N	\N
cms7542zv001cmr0157bimn17	Pitra Dosh Puja	Pitra Dosh Puja is a powerful Vedic ritual aimed at resolving the negative effects of Pitra Dosh, which occurs due to unsettled ancestral karmas affecting one’s life. This dosh manifests through planetary afflictions primarily involving the Sun, Rahu, and Ketu affecting the 9th house or related houses in the horoscope. It can cause financial instability, health problems, family discord, and repeated obstacles. The puja involves offerings, mantras, and specific rituals to honor ancestors, clear ancestral debts, and remove karmic blockages. Performing this puja restores peace, improves family relationships, promotes prosperity, enhances mental peace, and spiritual growth.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1hleDF317rd823E5ua4n0iWTdaa0fyoNF&sz=w1000	8500	Grah Dosh Nivaran Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.339	\N	\N	Resolves unsettled ancestral karmas (Pitra Dosh) linked to afflictions of the Sun, Rahu, and Ketu in the 9th house.	Restores family peace and harmony\nClears ancestral karmic blockages\nImproves financial stability\nEnhances mental peace\nSupports spiritual growth	\N	\N
