cms75433a0040mr01fpz0lrk2	Saraswati puja	Saraswati Puja, celebrated mainly during Vasant Panchami, is a revered Hindu ritual dedicated to Goddess Saraswati, the deity of knowledge, wisdom, learning, music, and arts. Devotees perform this puja by setting up an altar with Saraswati’s idol, adorned with white and yellow flowers, symbolizing purity and enlightenment. The rituals include chanting mantras, offering fruits, sweets, flowers, and worshipping musical instruments and books, symbolizing the pursuit of knowledge and creativity. It is believed that worshipping Goddess Saraswati purifies the mind, removes ignorance, and blesses devotees with intellect, creative skills, and success in education and arts.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1yrvEqMUQeHpXqEpXqrx4LvGySAVzijO5&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.462	\N	\N	Dedicated to Goddess Saraswati, deity of knowledge and arts, celebrated mainly during Vasant Panchami.	Enhances intellect and creativity\nPurifies the mind\nRemoves ignorance\nSupports success in education\nBoosts artistic and creative skills	\N	\N
cms75433e0043mr01utqeuxyu	Durga Puja	It includes rituals like Bodhon (invocation), Sandhi Puja (powerful worship at dusk), and Vijaya Dashami (immersion of the idol). Beyond religious significance, Durga Puja fosters community bonding, artistic expression, and cultural unity. The festival celebrates feminine power (Shakti), courage, and protection, inspiring values of righteousness, courage, and harmony among devotees.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1oewfEyyqhaQMEBXZgFoM14VCkUDVUQtk&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.466	\N	\N	A major festival celebrating the victory of Goddess Durga, invoking feminine power (Shakti), courage, and protection.	Fosters community bonding\nCelebrates courage and righteousness\nInvokes protection and strength\nEncourages cultural unity\nInspires harmony among devotees	\N	\N
cms75433i0046mr019xl5tu2m	Shiv Puja	Shiv Puja is a sacred Hindu ritual that involves devotional worship of Lord Shiva, the Supreme Being revered for his immense cosmic energy and transformative spiritual power. Through chants, offerings, and meditative practices, devotees aspire to invoke Shiva's presence, purify their minds, and foster spiritual advancement. The puja incorporates symbolic elements like flowers, incense, and mantras such as 'Om Namah Shivaya,' representing purity and surrender. By performing this puja with faith and sincerity, followers seek inner tranquility, enlightenment, protection from negativity, and the divine grace of Lord Shiva, embracing his role as both a destroyer of evil and a guide for spiritual awakening.​	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1uZeDl4_Ttv44-WZhFv0e7Rlc1P6gF_vi&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.47	\N	\N	Devotional worship of Lord Shiva to invoke his transformative cosmic power and spiritual grace.	Purifies the mind\nFosters spiritual advancement\nProvides protection from negativity\nBrings inner tranquility\nEncourages enlightenment and surrender	\N	\N
cms75433l0049mr01v664vr0y	Krishna Puja	Krishna Puja is a revered ritual honoring Lord Krishna, the embodiment of divine love, wisdom, and joy. It includes prayers, bhajans, lighting diyas, floral offerings, sandalwood application, aarti, milk bath, and distribution of prasad. Devotees chant Krishna’s names and mantras, seeking peace, prosperity, and spiritual upliftment. Performed on Janmashtami and other auspicious days, the puja symbolizes devotion, gratitude, and a deepened bond with the Lord.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1s5kRLYEAnDPAmUASrNkBv3tlKcaVS7zQ&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.474	\N	\N	Honors Lord Krishna, embodiment of divine love and wisdom, especially observed on Janmashtami.	Brings peace and spiritual upliftment\nDeepens devotion and gratitude\nInvokes divine love and joy\nEncourages prosperity\nStrengthens bond with the Lord	\N	\N
cms75433o004cmr01qtwzne2r	Lakshmi Puja	Lakshmi Puja is a traditional Hindu ritual dedicated to Goddess Lakshmi, the deity of wealth, fortune, and prosperity. It is most commonly performed during Diwali, but can also be conducted during other auspicious occasions. The puja involves thorough cleaning of the house, decorating with rangoli and lights, placing idols of Lakshmi and Ganesha, and offering flowers, sweets, turmeric, and kumkum. Devotees chant mantras, perform aarti, and light diyas to invite Lakshmi’s blessings, seeking the removal of poverty and obstacles. The ritual represents a heartfelt prayer for financial well-being, abundance, inner illumination, and harmony at home and in businesses.​	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1fFMM51qn3TvIjJD27skF1Ahs2_vU473N&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.477	\N	\N	Dedicated to Goddess Lakshmi, deity of wealth and prosperity, commonly performed during Diwali.	Removes poverty and obstacles\nAttracts financial well-being\nBrings abundance and harmony\nInvokes blessings for prosperity\nEnhances inner illumination	\N	\N
cms75433s004fmr01qy1jhxzr	5 Days Lakshmi Puja	The 5 Days Lakshmi Puja is a traditional celebration dedicated to Goddess Lakshmi, the deity of wealth, prosperity, and fortune. Observed over five auspicious days—beginning with Dhanteras and ending with Bhai Dooj—each day holds special rituals for inviting abundance and peace into homes. Devotees light lamps, perform aarti, and chant prayers to seek Goddess Lakshmi’s grace for financial stability, happiness, and spiritual growth.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1JVuhV2f01-whujn10d_OMJNGvbE0x4wT&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.48	\N	\N	A five-day celebration honoring Goddess Lakshmi, observed from Dhanteras to Bhai Dooj.	Invites abundance and prosperity\nBrings peace to the home\nSupports financial stability\nEncourages happiness\nPromotes spiritual growth	\N	\N
cms75433w004imr01v4vu2z55	Vishnu Puja	Vishnu Puja is a revered Hindu ritual dedicated to Lord Vishnu, the preserver and protector in the Hindu pantheon. Devotees perform this puja by chanting mantras, offering flowers, lighting lamps, and praying with devotion to seek the blessings of Vishnu for well-being. The ceremony is believed to bring safety, stability, peace, prosperity, and spiritual advances. Rituals may vary, but the core intention is to invite divine grace, overcome obstacles, and establish harmony in life and family.​	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1oIJ-q9BQ-RieHOrktBx-kJmyPRP9W6HU&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.484	\N	\N	Dedicated to Lord Vishnu, the preserver, to seek blessings for stability and well-being.	Brings safety and stability\nInvokes peace and prosperity\nSupports spiritual advancement\nOvercomes obstacles\nEstablishes family harmony	\N	\N
cms754340004lmr0180fzo030	Asht Lakhsmi Puja	Asht Lakshmi Puja worships the eight forms of Goddess Lakshmi, each granting a unique blessing: Adi Lakshmi (spiritual wealth), Dhana Lakshmi (financial prosperity), Dhanya Lakshmi (health), Gaja Lakshmi (power), Santana Lakshmi (family), Veera Lakshmi (courage), Vijaya Lakshmi (victory), and Vidya Lakshmi (knowledge). Through offerings and prayers, devotees seek harmony, success, and fulfillment in all areas of life.	https://drive.google.com/thumbnail?id=1vwv_yyhpGY8vza7G8X5LGDd58xcllyV1&sz=w1000	8500	Dev Puja	2026-07-30 06:36:07.489	\N	\N	Worships the eight forms of Goddess Lakshmi, each granting a distinct blessing.	Grants spiritual wealth\nAttracts financial prosperity\nSupports health and family well-being\nGrants courage and victory\nBestows knowledge and power	\N	\N
\.


